n a diocese species than a normal  selfing species  yep are you noticing any differences in  the flower structure when you increase  poisoning  uh so the question was are there any  differences in flower structure with an  increase in ploydy  i  personally have have not noticed that  but that's also anecdotal i don't know  if people have um done  you know inflorescence architecture  quantification and done proper  statistics to test that hypothesis but  it would be definitely an interesting  hypothesis to  test they do flower later oh right  um so so in these these diploid triploid  comparisons we do see that the triploids  generally flower later um which could be  an effect of being triploid it also  could be effects of flowering time genes  that are segregating in these  populations so when oregon cbd makes  their  their hybrids they use an autoflower  parent as their pollen parent so they  can  well for a variety of reasons but um  that is uh one of the the things that is  just innately part of all of their  hybrids um  so in in diploids um the hybrids have  one dose out of two from that auto  flower parent but in  triploids it's one dose out of three so  if this flowering time is is dosage  dependent it could be an effect of the  the genes in addition to the ploidy  alrighty i think we're running out of  time here but um  um i'll be around if anybody has any  questions and i'm excited to hear what  luis and jamie have to talk about at the  next stop  this has been a production of cornell  university on the web at cornell.edu


